## args
batch
--help
## exit
0
## stdout
Usage:
    xl batch --dry-run [<operations>]
    xl batch --schema

Apply multiple operations atomically from JSON.

USAGE:
  xl -f in.xlsx -s Sheet1 -o out.xlsx batch ops.json
  echo '[...]' | xl -f in.xlsx -s Sheet1 -o out.xlsx batch -
  xl batch --dry-run ops.json      # validate and summarise without a workbook
  xl batch --schema                # the document's JSON Schema (every op, field and alias)

OPERATIONS:
  put             {"op":"put","ref":"A1","value":1234.5,"format":"currency"}  (aliases: format|numFormat)
  putf            {"op":"putf","ref":"B2:B10","value":"=A2*2","from":"B2","format":"#,##0.0"}  (aliases: value|formula, from|anchor, format|numFormat)
  style           {"op":"style","range":"A1:D1","bold":true,"bg":"#4472C4","fg":"#FFFFFF","align":"center"}  (aliases: align|halign, numFormat|format)
  merge           {"op":"merge","range":"A1:D1"}
  unmerge         {"op":"unmerge","range":"A1:D1"}
  colwidth        {"op":"colwidth","col":"A","width":15.5}
  rowheight       {"op":"rowheight","row":1,"height":30}
  comment         {"op":"comment","ref":"A1","text":"Note","author":"User"}  [not with --stream]
  remove-comment  {"op":"remove-comment","ref":"A1"}  [not with --stream]
  hyperlink       {"op":"hyperlink","ref":"A1","target":"https://example.com"}  (aliases: target|url)  [not with --stream]
  clear           {"op":"clear","range":"A1:B10","all":true}  [not with --stream]
  col-hide        {"op":"col-hide","col":"C"}
  col-show        {"op":"col-show","col":"C"}
  row-hide        {"op":"row-hide","row":5}
  row-show        {"op":"row-show","row":5}
  group-rows      {"op":"group-rows","rows":"10:20","level":1,"collapsed":false}  [not with --stream]
  group-cols      {"op":"group-cols","cols":"E:H","level":1,"collapsed":false}  [not with --stream]
  ungroup-rows    {"op":"ungroup-rows","rows":"10:20"}  [not with --stream]
  ungroup-cols    {"op":"ungroup-cols","cols":"E:H"}  [not with --stream]
  autofit         {"op":"autofit","columns":"A:F"}  [not with --stream]
  add-sheet       {"op":"add-sheet","name":"Summary","after":"Sheet1"}  [not with --stream]
  rename-sheet    {"op":"rename-sheet","from":"Old","to":"New"}  [not with --stream]
  freeze          {"op":"freeze","ref":"B2"}  [not with --stream]
  unfreeze        {"op":"unfreeze"}  [not with --stream]
  copy            {"op":"copy","source":"A1:B2","target":"D1","valuesOnly":false}  [not with --stream]
  chart           {"op":"chart","type":"column","data":"B2:C4","categories":"A2:A4","seriesNames":"North,South","title":"Sales","legend":"right","at":"E2:K15"}  [not with --stream]
  sheet-view      {"op":"sheet-view","gridlines":false,"zoom":85}  [not with --stream]
  tab-color       {"op":"tab-color","color":"#1F4E79"}  [not with --stream]
  autofilter      {"op":"autofilter","range":"A1:M29"}  [not with --stream]
  page-setup      {"op":"page-setup","orientation":"landscape","fitToWidth":1,"fitToHeight":0}  [not with --stream]
  header-footer   {"op":"header-footer","oddFooter":"&LConfidential&RPage &P of &N"}  [not with --stream]
  cf              {"op":"cf","range":"A1:A10","rule":"cellIs:greaterThan:100","bold":true,"bg":"#FFC7CE","fg":"#9C0006"}  [not with --stream]

Every op except add-sheet/rename-sheet accepts "sheet": the sheet for its unqualified refs
(a sheet-qualified ref wins, then "sheet", then -s/--sheet). Property names are accepted in
camelCase or kebab-case. put/putf "format" is explicit and replaces the cell's number format.

STYLE PROPERTIES (style op):
  Font:      bold, italic, underline, fg, fontSize, fontName
  Fill:      bg (background color, e.g., "#FFFF00" or "yellow")
  Align:     align (left/center/right), valign (top/middle/bottom), wrap
  Format:    numFormat (general/number/currency/percent/date/text or an Excel format code)
  Border:    border (all), borderTop/Right/Bottom/Left, borderColor
  Mode:      replace (true=replace style, false=merge with existing)

EXAMPLE:
  [
    {"op": "put", "ref": "A1", "value": "Revenue Report"},
    {"op": "style", "range": "A1:D1", "bold": true, "bg": "#4472C4", "fg": "#FFFFFF", "align": "center"},
    {"op": "merge", "range": "A1:D1"},
    {"op": "colwidth", "col": "A", "width": 25},
    {"op": "put", "ref": "A2", "value": "Q1"},
    {"op": "put", "ref": "B2", "value": 1000},
    {"op": "putf", "ref": "C2", "value": "=B2*1.1"}
  ]

Operations execute in order. Use "-" to read from stdin.
Use --dry-run to validate JSON without writing; --schema prints the JSON Schema.

Options and flags:
    --help
        Display this help text.
    --dry-run
        Validate batch JSON and show summary without writing
    --schema
        Print the JSON Schema of the batch document (every op, field and alias) and exit
## stderr
